<title>GREECE: GREECE PLANS GREATER AUTONOMY FOR PENSION FUNDS - MIN.</title>
<headline>GREECE PLANS GREATER AUTONOMY FOR PENSION FUNDS - MIN.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek pension funds, which invest mainly in T-bills, will be given greater autonomy to invest in the stock market, National Economy Minister Yannos Papandoniou told Reuters Financial Television in an interview.</p>
<p>&quot;Our policy is to extend the ability of pension funds to gradually invest in stocks. This has become true with shares of OTE telecom and it is our intention to grant greater autonomy to pension funds,&quot; Papandoniou told RFTV on Monday.</p>
</text>
